Subject: WebKit: PlayStation page C API fixes for the PS5 shell

WKPageSetDrawsTransparentBackground() exposes
WebPageProxy::setBackgroundColor(transparent) to C clients, so the HTML
chrome can be painted over the page with real alpha (the PlayStation C
API has no drawsBackground setter). The Skia background fill in
WKPagePaint is clipped to the unpainted rect instead of clearing the
whole surface.

WKPageHandleKeyboardEvent forwards the WKKeyboardEvent modifiers and
text (so Return fires keypress and submits forms); virtualKeyCode is a
WPE keysym, as before.

WKPageHandleWheelEvent sends one precise-pixel 2D (smooth) wheel event
and nothing for a zero delta. Before, each axis became a separate line
tick: the magnitude was lost and a 0 delta still scrolled one line.

WKPageHandleMouseEvent gives every event a real monotonic time and the
pressed-button bits in the modifiers, as the WPE backends do. libwpe's
WebEventFactory computes clickCount from the time: with a constant 0,
every press within 5 px of the previous one became a double/triple
click (word/paragraph selection); without button bits, mousedown and
pointerdown reported buttons == 0.

PlayStationWebView::enterFullScreen() records the fullscreen state when
the client accepts: nothing called willEnterFullScreen(), so
m_isFullScreen stayed false, exitFullScreen() never reached the client
and WKViewRequestExitFullScreen() did nothing.
